            <div xml:id="d452">

                <pb facs="0632" n="552" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg552"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851.5151/972: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-09-19T11:00:00+01:00">September 19,
                            1936—11 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 19—9:17 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>893. For the Secretary of the Treasury from Cochran. Reference to my 892,
                    September 18, 10 p.m., Baumgartner telephoned me this morning that Leith-Ross
                    had also objected to inclusion of reference to eventual return to gold standard
                    and had indicated that certain revision in phraseology would be necessary to
                    suit British public. In final interview before Leith-Ross’s departure for London
                    Minister of Finance Auriol stressed to him his insistence upon a simultaneous
                    common declaration.</p>
                <p>It is arranged for me to communicate to Baumgartner tonight or tomorrow morning
                    any suggestions that may be received from you in the meantime. [Cochran.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
